IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cda-nouns`

-- Criminal Damage Act 1971: FIXTURES shared by the test modules.
-- Layer 1 support. No rules and no assertions here: only named example facts, each
-- named for the situation it stands for, so that an assertion reads as a sentence.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `Beliefs (section 5(3))`

`an honest and justified belief` MEANS Belief WITH
    `honestly held` IS TRUE
    `justified` IS TRUE

`an honest but unjustified belief` MEANS Belief WITH
    `honestly held` IS TRUE
    `justified` IS FALSE

`a justified belief that was not honestly held` MEANS Belief WITH
    `honestly held` IS FALSE
    `justified` IS TRUE

`no belief held` MEANS Belief WITH
    `honestly held` IS FALSE
    `justified` IS FALSE

§§ `Lawful excuse facts (section 5)`

`no lawful excuse` MEANS `Lawful excuse facts` WITH
    `belief that the persons believed to be entitled to consent had consented` IS `no belief held`
    `belief that those persons would have consented if they had known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances` IS `no belief held`
    `purpose of protecting property belonging to the accused or another` IS FALSE
    `purpose of protecting a right or interest in property` IS FALSE
    `purpose of protecting a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise` IS FALSE
    `the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS FALSE
    `belief that the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS `no belief held`
    `belief that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` IS `no belief held`
    `belief that the means of protection adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable having regard to all the circumstances` IS `no belief held`
    `a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2)` IS FALSE

`an honest and justified belief that consent had been given` MEANS `Lawful excuse facts` WITH
    `belief that the persons believed to be entitled to consent had consented` IS `an honest and justified belief`
    `belief that those persons would have consented if they had known of the destruction or damage and its circumstances` IS `no belief held`
    `purpose of protecting property belonging to the accused or another` IS FALSE
    `purpose of protecting a right or interest in property` IS FALSE
    `purpose of protecting a right or privilege in or over land, whether created by grant, licence or otherwise` IS FALSE
    `the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS FALSE
    `belief that the right or interest was vested in the accused or another` IS `no belief held`
    `belief that the property, right or interest was in immediate need of protection` IS `no belief held`
    `belief that the means of protection adopted or proposed were or would be reasonable having regard to all the circumstances` IS `no belief held`
    `a lawful excuse or defence recognised by law apart from section 5(2)` IS FALSE

`an honest and justified belief that consent would have been given` MEANS `Lawful excuse facts` WITH
